truct operationalizations:**\n  - *Rare pattern* [LOCKED/your decision]: a joint feature-value combination of 2\u20134 features occurring in <1% of rows (base prevalence set at 0.1%, 0.5%, 1.0%). Rows are the recoverable unit.\n  - *Identify* [LOCKED/your decision]: quantitative recovery of planted ground truth on synthetic data (primary) + qualitative characterization of surfaced patterns on real data (secondary).\n- **Hypotheses:**\n  - H1: Docta's pattern-level recall on planted patterns exceeds the permutation null and at least one baseline.\n  - H2: Docta's recovery degrades gracefully as pattern size increases (2\u21924 features) and as prevalence decreases, relative to baselines.\n  - H3 (falsifiable): on real data, Docta surfaces human-interpretable low-frequency combinations not trivially captured by a raw frequency cutoff.\n\n## II. Docta: Definition, Assumed Interface, and Setup\nPer your decision, Docta is treated as a **given black-box method**. [MY DECISION, not a fixed brief requirement]\n- **(a) Assumed interface (input-output contract):**\n  - Input: a tabular dataset, rows \u00d7 columns, mixed types (categorical + numeric; numeric optionally binned).\n  - Output: a set of identified rare patterns; each pattern represented as a joint feature-value combination or a small row-cluster, each carrying a confidence/score. A per-row score is also assumed available (needed for row-level AUC).\n- **(b) Explicit assumption flag:** The exact API, function names, hyperparameters (e.g., minimum support, pattern-size range, scoring normalization), and internal mechanism are an **ASSUMPTION** and **must be validated against Docta's actual documentation before execution.** No source documentation exists in this workspace and network is disabled, so nothing here asserts Docta's true behavior.\n- **(c) Structural agnosticism:** The entire experimental structure (planted patterns, ground-truth matching, metrics, baselines, controls) depends **only** on the input-outp